{"levels":[{"n":1,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 0.47 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x\nMY MOVES: hand walk pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h5 2o:h7 3o:h7 4o:h7 5o:h7 6o:h7 7o:h5 | home after 1 touch: walk 9% | after 2: walk 12% | if held: pull 48%\nGOAL: score 1 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score on your first raid; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 99/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the raid: pick a defender, Hand Touch him and walk back over the midline. Seven rookies, 3 raids, 1 point needed — the only lesson is that a touch only counts once you are home.","mechanics":["hand touch","walk home"],"optimal":4,"branching":8,"trap":0,"explored":293},{"n":2,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: T T o o T T T · grip 0.20 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x\nMY MOVES: hand walk pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h15 2T:h16 3o:h8 4o:h8 5T:h16 6T:h20 7T:h15 | home after 1 touch: walk 23% | after 2: walk 29% | if held: pull 47%\nGOAL: score 2 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Never get caught; No empty raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 97/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Two rookies stand in the gap between five big Thigh-holders (T). A Hand Touch on a T, or beside him, gets you grabbed; the rookie pair in slots 3-4 is the safe touch. Aha: read the gap, not the defender. 2 points in 3 raids.","mechanics":["hand touch","walk home","thigh-holders"],"optimal":6,"branching":8,"trap":0,"explored":6405},{"n":3,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: o o T T T T T · grip 0.18 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h2 2o:h7 3T:h14 4T:h18 5T:h18 6T:h18 7T:h14 | home after 1 touch: walk 20%, dash 8% | after 2: walk 26%, dash 10% | if held: pull 47%\nGOAL: score 3 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Never get caught; Score 4 points\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 88/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the way home: five Thigh-holders stand between you and the midline and only the two left-hand men are rookies. The touch on the corner rookie is safe either way; the walk home past five slow-reaching T's is the risk (READ: walk home held about 2.5x as often as the Dash). Aha: the way home is a choice too — touch the safe rookie, then burst home with the Dash. 3 points in 4 raids.","mechanics":["hand touch","walk home","dash home","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":4,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Village raider\": s 0.10 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 27/thigh 70; toe: ankle 71/thigh 25 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 32/thigh 56 | his touch lands 73% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 4 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 87/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"First defence, in one drill: select a defender beside the raider's target, pick the hold, and press on the tackle ring. The village raider telegraphs his touch — a Hand Touch (high) or a Toe Touch (low). The Ankle Hold catches a Toe, the Thigh Hold catches a Hand; the wrong hold misses about 3 times in 4, and 'Hold' (no tackle) just hands him the point. Aha: watch his move, then match the hold. Stop 3 of his 5 raids, concede no more than 4.","mechanics":["ankle hold","thigh hold","tackle ring","read the raider's move"],"optimal":null,"branching":11,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":5,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: o o T T T o o · grip 0.15 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h2 2o:h6 3T:h12 4T:h15 5T:h12 6o:h6 7o:h2 | home after 1 touch: walk 12%, dash 5% | after 2: walk 16%, dash 7% | if held: pull 48%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Win within 2 raids; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 83/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach greed: a rookie pair stands on each corner around a wall of three Thigh-holders. 4 points in 3 raids means at least one raid must take two touches — but every touch already made raises the next touch's risk by a third and makes the way home deeper (READ: home after 1 touch vs after 2). Aha: be greedy only along a rookie pair — the corner first, then his rookie neighbour away from the T, then Dash home; a second touch next to a T is where raids end.","mechanics":["hand touch","dash home","raid depth","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":6,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Village raider\": s 0.24 · Easy · touches hand · home walk · up to 1 touch\nON SCREEN: cover ring (target 82% / neighbours 100% / two away 55%)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 25/thigh 63 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 28/thigh 49 | his touch lands 76% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 89/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist: not WHICH hold but WHO tackles. This raider only Hand Touches and walks home, so the Thigh Hold is always the right hold; the cover ring on screen shows who should make it — the man he touches tackles at 82% of full strength (he is off balance), his neighbour, the cover, at 100%, two away at 55%. Aha: let the cover make the tackle, never the man being touched. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["thigh hold","cover position","defender select"],"optimal":null,"branching":11,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":7,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: T T o T o T T · grip 0.36 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h26 2T:h27 3o:h20 4T:h20 5o:h20 6T:h27 7T:h26 | home after 1 touch: walk 36%, dash 15% | after 2: walk 46%, dash 20% | if held: pull 45%\nGOAL: score 3 | FAIL: raider out 3x | STARS: Break free from a hold; Win within 4 raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 84/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Five Thigh-holders with strong grips around one rookie: even good raids get held here. Held raiders play the struggle — the pull-away breaks free about half the time, and the defender holding you counts as touched when you do. Aha: a hold is not the end — keep raiding the rookie gap and rip loose when grabbed. Score 3 in 5 raids; caught 3 times and it's over.","mechanics":["hand touch","dash home","struggle (pull-away)","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":8,"grid":"[Match · breather · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: o T o o T o o · grip 0.60 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 3 raids / 3 defences\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Fair raider\": s 0.32 · Easy · touches hand · home walk · up to 1 touch\nMOMENT (ref, after raid 2): \"LOBBY! Their Thigh-holder stepped out of bounds — the referee sends him off. Re-read the mat.\" → slot 2 sent off\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h19 2T:h31 3o:h21 4o:h21 5T:h31 6o:h21 7o:h7 | home after 1 touch: walk 31%, dash 16% | after 2: walk 40%, dash 21% | if held: pull 42%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 23/thigh 60 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 26/thigh 45 | his touch lands 78% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Win by 4\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 84/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Breather and the first real match flow: 3 raids each against a gentle village side (two Thigh-holders, a Hand-Touch-only raider), the sides swapping after every raid. After the first two raids the referee steps in: LOBBY — their Thigh-holder in slot 2 stepped out of bounds and is sent off the mat, so the gap you have been raiding changes shape. Aha: after a referee's call, re-read the mat before you raid. Win the segment by 1; 3 stars for winning by 4.","mechanics":["hand touch","dash home","ankle hold","thigh hold","alternating raids","referee's call"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":9,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: T o o T o T o · grip 0.60 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Village raider\": s 0.17 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nMOMENT (reversal, after raid 4): \"REVERSAL! Their coach swaps the shape: Thigh-holders into the gaps — and their raider now only Toe-touches and Dashes home.\" → OPP MAT becomes o T T o T T o → CPU raider mv toe, ret dash\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h30 2o:h21 3o:h21 4T:h31 5o:h31 6T:h31 7o:h19 | home after 1 touch: walk 40%, dash 18% | after 2: walk 49%, dash 24% | if held: pull 42%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 26/thigh 66; toe: ankle 68/thigh 24 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 30/thigh 52; dash: ankle 48/thigh 25 | his touch lands 74% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 2+ | STARS: Win by 4; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 80/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Combine both halves of chapter 1, then flip them: 4 raids each. At first T's guard both corners and the centre, so raid the gaps and Dash home, and their raider mixes Hand and Toe, so match the hold. After two raids each their coach reverses everything: the T's move into the old gaps (rookies now at the corners and the centre) and their raider switches to Toe Touches and Dash home only. Aha: a reversal is a new puzzle — re-read both ends (your safe touch moves, and one Ankle Hold now beats both his touch and his way home). Win by 2.","mechanics":["hand touch","dash home","ankle hold","thigh hold","return tackle","thigh-holders","mid-match reversal"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":10,"grid":"[Comeback · spike · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: T T o T o T T · grip 0.31 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 11-13\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Village captain\": s 0.11 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h23 2T:h24 3o:h18 4T:h18 5o:h18 6T:h24 7T:h23 | home after 1 touch: walk 33%, dash 13% | after 2: walk 41%, dash 17% | if held: pull 46%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 27/thigh 69; toe: ankle 71/thigh 25 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 32/thigh 56; dash: ankle 51/thigh 27 | his touch lands 73% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Concede at most 3\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 32/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 76/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Spike: 15:00 of the second half, 11-13 down, 4 raids each left against the village's best raider. Two points is a lot in 8 raids: you need one stop and steady touches, and a second touch only when the gap beside your first is a rookie. Win by 1.","mechanics":["hand touch","dash home","struggle (pull-away)","ankle hold","thigh hold","comeback"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":11,"grid":"[Full Match · boss · Ch1 Village Mat] OPP MAT: o T T o T T o · grip 0.60 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate raids 00:00→12:00 (~17 raids in all, ~9 each, half-time swap at 06:00)\nMY MOVES: hand walk dash pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Bholu, the greedy captain\": s 0.50 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home dash · up to 2 touches · personality: goes for all 2 touches 80% of raids\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h19 2T:h40 3T:h40 4o:h31 5T:h40 6T:h40 7o:h19 | home after 1 touch: walk 47%, dash 21% | after 2: walk 57%, dash 27% | if held: pull 42%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 52; toe: ankle 53/thigh 19 | vs his way home — dash: ankle 34/thigh 18 | his touch lands 82% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Win by 6\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 90/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Chapter boss and the first whole match, kept short: the Village Final as a mini-Blitz of 2x6 game minutes (~17 raids in all) with a half-time swap. Their captain Bholu has a personality you can read: he is greedy — he goes for two touches on 8 raids in 10 and always Dashes home. Aha: his second touch and his Dash are your chances — tackle his next target with the cover, or Ankle his Dash home; on your raids, raid the rookie gaps and Dash past the T's. Win the match.","mechanics":["hand touch","dash home","struggle (pull-away)","ankle hold","thigh hold","cover position","full match"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":12,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: T T T T T T T · grip 0.29 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h21/t3 2T:h28/t5 3T:h28/t5 4T:h28/t5 5T:h28/t5 6T:h28/t5 7T:h21/t3 | home after 1 touch: walk 39%, dash 15% | after 2: walk 49%, dash 20% | if held: pull 46%\nGOAL: score 3 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Never get caught; Win within 3 raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 82/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (be