n":13,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · twist · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A T A o T T A · grip 0.28 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h9/t15 2T:h16/t16 3A:h10/t16 4o:h11/t10 5T:h22/t4 6T:h22/t11 7A:h9/t15 | home after 1 touch: walk 24%, dash 10% | after 2: walk 31%, dash 13% | if held: pull 46%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Never get caught; Win within 3 raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 90/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist: Ankle-catchers (A) on both corners and slot 3 wait for your Toe Touch, the T's wait for your Hand. The READ row shows the counter for each slot: Hand on an A, Toe on a T — and slot 2, a T between two A's, is the one to avoid with both. Aha: every defender has a counter. 4 points in 5 raids.","mechanics":["toe touch","hand touch","dash home","thigh-holders","ankle-catchers"],"optimal":null,"branching":16,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":14,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: T B B o B B T · grip 0.62 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky), o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull\nON SCREEN: Blocker wall drawn on the midline; the Dash gem carries a WALLED tag with its real % (shown, never a hidden trap)\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h32/t8 2B:h25/t11 3B:h13/t11 4o:h12/t10 5B:h13/t11 6B:h25/t11 7T:h32/t8 | home after 1 touch: walk 46%, dash 69%, dubki 15% | after 2: walk 56%, dash 79%, dubki 20% | if held: pull 42%\nGOAL: score 3, 1x lowMove | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with Dubki twice; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 89/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Four Blockers (B) form a wall on the midline — the screen shows it: before you pick the way home the B's link arms across the midline and the Dash gem is drawn against the wall, so a Dash into them (held most of the time, READ) is shown on its gem with a WALLED tag — never a hidden trap. The Dubki ducks under their arms and the T's reach. Aha: dubki under a reach. Score 3 points with at least one Dubki or Toe Touch scoring.","mechanics":["dubki","toe touch","hand touch","blocker wall","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":17,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":15,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District sprinter\": s 0.23 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nBLOCK WINDOW: ×1.15 (wider timing for the teaching unit)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 25/thigh 64; toe: ankle 65/thigh 23 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 28/thigh 49/block 41; dash: ankle 45/thigh 24/block 77 | his touch lands 76% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 91/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the Block: the district sprinter telegraphs his way home — mostly a Dash, sometimes a walk. Against a Dash, let the touch go and form the Block on the midline (its timing window is a little wider in this first lesson, READ); against a walk the Block is weak and the Thigh Hold is the stop. Aha: defend the way home, not the touch — and read WHICH way home before you build the wall. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["block (defensive wall)","ankle hold","thigh hold","return tackle"],"optimal":6,"branching":7,"trap":0,"explored":19896},{"n":16,"grid":"[Match · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A o T o T o A · grip 0.70 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 8-7 · empty raids 1/0\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District raider\": s 0.45 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h7/t34 2o:h24/t24 3T:h36/t10 4o:h36/t10 5T:h36/t10 6o:h24/t24 7A:h7/t34 | home after 1 touch: walk 39%, dash 19%, dubki 43% | after 2: walk 49%, dash 25%, dubki 53% | if held: pull 41%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 54; toe: ankle 55/thigh 19 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 22/thigh 39/block 29; dash: ankle 36/thigh 19/block 55 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 2+ | STARS: Win by 4; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 83/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the empty-raid counter: you lead 8-7 and already have 1 empty raid. The mat is soft but for its two Ankle-catcher corners. An empty raid is safe — touching nobody keeps you deep in your own half — but the third in a row is Do-or-Die, so after one more empty raid you MUST touch. Aha: one patient empty raid is a weapon, two is a risk. 4 raids each, win by 2.","mechanics":["empty-raid counter","toe touch","dubki","block (defensive wall)","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":17,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":17,"grid":"[Do-or-Die Drill · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A o B B B o A · grip 0.18 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), o rookie, B blocker (Dash risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x · empty raids 2/0\nMY MOVES: hand toe walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h2/t10 2o:h3/t7 3B:h4/t3 4B:h4/t4 5B:h4/t3 6o:h3/t7 7A:h2/t10 | home after 1 touch: walk 10%, dash 22%, dubki 14% | after 2: walk 13%, dash 29%, dubki 18% | if held: pull 48%\nGOAL: score 3, 1x dodWin | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score 4 points; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Straight after the empty-raid counter: two empty raids already: your next raid is Do-or-Die and an empty return puts you out. Ankle-catchers on the corners, a Blocker wall in the middle. The wall shuts the Dash home and the corner A's read the Dubki, so the safe way back is a plain walk (READ). The trade-off: the safe touch (Hand on an A, walk home) wins the Do-or-Die but scores only 1, and the goal is 3 points in 3 raids — so after the Do-or-Die one free raid may take a greedy second touch, a third riskier and deeper from home. The Do-or-Die IS the lesson: win it first. Aha: survive the Do-or-Die with the safe touch, then spend the greed on a free raid after it. Win the Do-or-Die raid and score 3 in 3 raids.","mechanics":["do-or-die raid","toe touch","hand touch","dubki","ankle-catchers","blocker wall"],"optimal":null,"branching":17,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":18,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: o T T o T T o · grip 0.32 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h11/t3 2T:h24/t5 3T:h24/t5 4o:h18/t5 5T:h24/t5 6T:h24/t5 7o:h11/t3 bonus:4 | home after 1 touch: walk 28%, dash 12%, dubki 7% | after 2: walk 36%, dash 16%, dubki 9% | if held: pull 46%\nGOAL: score 4, 2x bonus | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Earn 3 bonus points; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 80/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move 