es: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist: now THEIR raider is on 2 empty raids, so his first raid is Do-or-Die — he must touch someone, so his telegraph is always a real attempt and an empty raid puts him out. The extra consequence: one of your side is already out, so a stop revives him (every point revives one, first out, first back) and every touch he lands sends another of yours off; fall to 3 on the mat and the trial is lost. Aha: a forced raider is predictable — punish his Do-or-Die with the matching hold and win your men back. Stop 2 of his 4 raids, concede no more than 5.","mechanics":["do-or-die raid","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)","revival"],"optimal":4,"branching":7,"trap":0,"explored":788},{"n":20,"grid":"[Match · spike · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A o T B T o A · grip 0.70 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 13-13 · empty raids 1/1\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District star\": s 0.49 · Easy · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h7/t34 2o:h24/t24 3T:h37/t11 4B:h37/t12 5T:h37/t11 6o:h24/t24 7A:h7/t34 bonus:43 | home after 1 touch: walk 43%, dash 39%, dubki 43% | after 2: walk 53%, dash 48%, dubki 53% | if held: pull 41%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 52; toe: ankle 54/thigh 19; bonus: ankle 33/thigh 22 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 21/thigh 38/block 27; dash: ankle 34/thigh 18/bl