 Match · boss · Ch2 District Cup] OPP MAT: A T T B T T A · grip 0.82 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate raids 30:00→40:00 (~14 raids in all, ~7 each) · start score 16-17\nMY MOVES: hand toe bonus walk dash dubki pull | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block hold\nCPU RAIDER \"District captain\": s 0.50 · Easy · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h25/t39 2T:h51/t28 3T:h52/t13 4B:h42/t14 5T:h52/t13 6T:h51/t28 7A:h25/t39 bonus:48 | home after 1 touch: walk 63%, dash 49%, dubki 49% | after 2: walk 74%, dash 59%, dubki 60% | if held: pull 40%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 20/thigh 52; toe: ankle 53/thigh 19; bonus: ankle 32/thigh 22 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 21/thigh 37/block 27; dash: ankle 34/thigh 18/block 52; dubki: ankle 38/thigh 6/block 9 | his touch lands 82% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 4; Win by 7\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Chapter boss with a Do-or-Die finish, kept to one session: the last 10 minutes of the District Final (~15 raids), one down at 16-17. A, T and B defenders and a raider who hops the bonus and Dubkis home; Do-or-Die is live on both sides, so the empty raids you spend early decide who is forced at the end. Aha: manage the empties like a clock — spend patience while level, never while behind. Win the match.","mechanics":["full match","do-or-die raid","bonus line","toe touch","dubki","block (defensive wall)","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":23,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: R o R o R o R · grip 0.65 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h21/t19/k4 2o:h23/t21 3R:h23/t21/k6 4o:h23/t21 5R:h23/t21/k6 6o:h23/t21 7R:h21/t19/k4 bonus:66 | home after 1 touch: walk 27%, dash 12%, dubki 25% | after 2: walk 35%, dash 16%, dubki 32% | if held: pull 46%\nGOAL: score 3, 2x kick | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Win within 3 raids; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 33/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 73/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the Backward Kick: Rushers (R) charge the raider and hold about a third of Hand or Toe Touches near them, but a Backward Kick tags a charging R at a fraction of that risk (READ). Aha: let the rusher come to you. Score 2 Kicks and 3 points in 4 raids.","mechanics":["backward kick","rusher defenders","hand touch","toe touch","dash home"],"optimal":null,"branching":22,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":24,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: T T C C T T T · grip 0.77 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h47/t9 2T:h50/t14 3C:h33/t17 4C:h33/t17 5T:h50/t14 6T:h57/t12 7T:h47/t9 bonus:17 | home after 1 touch: walk 71%, dash 48%, dubki 17% | after 2: walk 81%, dash 58%, dubki 22% | if held: pull 40%, lunge 40%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 3x | STARS: Escape a hold; Score 5 points\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 90/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the Escape lunge: strong-grip T's and a chained pair (C C) will hold you. Walking or dashing home past them is held most of the time — only the Dubki gets home reliably (READ). When held, the lunge for the line is strong held shallow (0-1 touches) and fades with every touch; held deep, the stamina pull-away is the better struggle. Aha: Dubki home, and if held: shallow → lunge, deep → pull. Score 4 in 4 raids; caught 3 times and it's over.","mechanics":["escape lunge","struggle (pull-away)","chain links","thigh-holders","hand touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":25,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o o o o 