egend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the Super Tackle: you have only 3 on the mat, so any tackle is worth 2 — but he goes for two touches, and lose all 3 and the all-out gives them +2. Choose WHICH of your three makes the tackle — the one beside his target (cover), never the man he touches. Aha: three defenders are a threat, not a weakness. Land a Super Tackle within 4 raids and concede no more than 2 (his two-touch raid can cost two at once).","mechanics":["super tackle","all-out","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)","defender rush"],"optimal":2,"branching":10,"trap":0,"explored":27},{"n":27,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · twist · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o R T R T o R · grip 0.65 · KEY: o rookie, R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h14/t13 2R:h34/t21/k9 3T:h43/t22 4R:h43/t22/k11 5T:h38/t16 6o:h28/t15 7R:h21/t19/k4 bonus:53 | home after 1 touch: walk 42%, dash 18%, dubki 23% | after 2: walk 52%, dash 23%, dubki 29% | if held: pull 42%, lunge 41%\nGOAL: score 4, 1x kick | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with 2 kicks; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist, one idea only: state sides scout you. A touch move or way home you used on your PREVIOUS raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and its real % rises (READ row). Rushers sit beside Thigh-holders, so the Kick on a charging R and the Toe on a T are both good touches, and the Dash and the walk both get you home. Aha: the safest move is the one you did not just use — alternate Kick and Toe, Dash and walk. Score 4 in 4 raids with at least one Kick.","mechanics":["defence reads repeats","backward kick","rusher defenders","thigh-holders","toe touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":21,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":28,"grid":"[Super Challenge · teach · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: - - o o - T - · grip 0.81 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 3o:h9/t8 4o:h27/t11 6T:h38/t9 | home after 1 touch: walk 21%, dash 10%, dubki 7% | after 2: walk 28%, dash 13%, dubki 10% | if held: pull 40%, lunge 39%\nGOAL: 1x allOut | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: All-out within 2 raids; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the all-out: three are left — two rookies and a Thigh-holder. Touch all three out (a greedy 2-touch raid along the rookie pair, then the T with a Toe) and the all-out is +2 with their whole side coming back. No scouting on this short drill (no SCOUTED tags): the only question is the order of the touches. Aha: finish the job — a lone survivor revives them. Inflict the all-out within 3 raids.","mechanics":["all-out","hand touch","toe touch","backward kick","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":9,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":29,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State kicker\": s 0.65 · Easy · touches hand/kick · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27; kick: ankle 16/thigh 19/rush 4 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 44/rush 10 | his touch lands 86% if untackled | Hold (step back) vs a real Kick: it finds nobody 65% of the time\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 4 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Concede at most 3\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 86/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist on the kick: now THEIR raider touches once and then Backward-Kicks the defender who chases him — his telegraph shows KICK before he turns, so you always see it coming. Chasing a kick is the trap (no hold catches it well, a Rush almost never). The counter is to step back: if nobody steps in (Hold), his kick finds nobody to tag 65% of the time, and his way home is still yours to Block. When he shows a Hand, Thigh Hold the touch as usual. The cost of the step-back: Hold never stops him on the touch, so the stop must come on his way home. Aha: never chase a kicker — step back, then beat his way home. Stop 2 of 5, concede no more than 4.","mechanics":["CPU backward kick","defender rush","thigh hold","ankle hold","block (defensive wall)"],"optimal":4,"branching":16,"trap":0,"explored":2157},{"n":30,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch3 State League] OPP MAT: R T R B R T R · grip 0.80 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"State raider\": s 0.56 · Easy · touches hand/bonus · home dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h38/t24/k8 2T:h50/t26 3R:h41/t27/k12 4B:h30/t27 5R:h41/t27/k12 6T:h50/t26 7R:h38/t24/k8 bonus:73 | home after 1 touch: walk 55%, dash 43%, dubki 31% | after 2: walk 66%, dash 53%, dubki 40% | if held: pull 40%, lunge 39%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 49/rush 29; bonus: ankle 31/thigh 21/rush 54 | vs his way home — dash: ankle 31/thigh 17/block 48/rush 11 | his touch lands 84% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 2+ | STARS: Win by 4; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 76/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' 