en 18 market 20-32; Anchor(anchor) open 14 market 16-26\nGOAL: buy Raider + Corner + Anchor | STARS: Keep 15 lakh in the purse; Keep 25 lakh in the purse\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 38/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 71/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the auction: 6 lots — a star Raider and a cheap one, two Corners, two Anchors — and an 85-lakh purse against AI franchises. The star goes for 45-60, so buying him leaves barely enough for a Corner and an Anchor and nothing for the stars; the budget Raider, a Corner and an Anchor cost about 55. The purse helper on screen shows what is still needed and the cheapest squad left. Aha: price the whole squad, not the lot — a lot you pass on has a cheaper twin later. Buy a Raider, a Corner and an Anchor.","mechanics":["auction","player roles","purse"],"optimal":9,"branching":2,"trap":0,"explored":5400},{"n":35,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o o o o o T (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League raider\": s 0.45 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 54/rush 32; toe: ankle 56/thigh 20/rush 34 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 23/thigh 39/block 29/rush 17; dash: ankle 36/thigh 19/block 55/rush 12 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 71/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach specialists: your left corner is an Ankle specialist (A, ankle ×1.25), your right corner a Thigh specialist (T, thigh ×1.25). The raider attacks anywhere with Hand or Toe. Aha: switch to the specialist whose hold matches his move when he is in range. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["hold specialists","ankle hold","thigh hold","cover position","defender select"],"optimal":null,"branching":13,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":36,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o o K o o T (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League raider\": s 0.36 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch\nON SCREEN: Anchor range ring (±1 slot)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 22/thigh 58/rush 34; toe: ankle 59/thigh 21/rush 36 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 25/thigh 43/block 31/rush 18; dash: ankle 39/thigh 21/block 59/rush 14; dubki: ankle 44/thigh 7/block 10/rush 18 | his touch lands 79% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 89/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the Anchor, with his range drawn on the mat: K in slot 4 multiplies every hold by 1.15 and his tackles rarely slip, and the shaded ring shows his range — slots 3-5, the target and one either side. Inside the ring the Anchor is the tackler whatever the move; outside it he is too far (half strength), so at the corners use the corner specialist when his hold matches the move, the defender beside the target when it does not. Aha: the specialists need the right read, the Anchor only needs the raider inside his ring. Stop 3 of 5.","mechanics":["anchor","hold specialists","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)"],"optimal":null,"branching":13,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":37,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o o K o o T (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Feinting raider\": s 0.65 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch · feints 30% · TELL on 60% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 85%)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 43/rush 10; dubki: ankle 31/thigh 5/block 8/rush 13 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Concede at most 3\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 88/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist: this raider feints — 3 raids in 10 the telegraphed move is not the real one — but feints have a tell: on 6 of 10 feints his hips turn first and the telegraph flickers (FEINT? on screen), so a flickering telegraph is a lie and a clean one is true about 85% of the time. Aha: trust a clean telegraph and counter it; against a flicker, use the all-round Anchor or an Ankle on his way home (it covers Dash and Dubki). Stop 2 of 5, concede no more than 5.","mechanics":["feints","anchor","hold specialists","block (defensive wall)","ankle hold","thigh hold"],"optimal":4,"branching":16,"trap":0,"explored":1537},{"n":38,"grid":"[Match · practise · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: A T B o B T A · grip 1.08 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky), o rookie · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~6 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: A T o K o T A (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences · start score 20-18\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League raider\": s 0.65 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h31/t47 2T:h50/t35 3B:h37/t17 4o:h19/t17 5B:h37/t17 6T:h50/t35 7A:h31/t47 bonus:58 | home after 1 touch: walk 62%, dash 69%, dubki 59% | after 2: walk 73%, dash 80%, dubki 70% | if held: pull 37%, lunge 36%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 43/rush 10 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | FAIL: trail by > 2 | STARS: Win by 3; No empty raids\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 84/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"A different kind of goal — game management: you lead 20-18 with 4 raids each to go, and the trial is lost if you ever trail by more than 2. Your specialist squad defends (A corners, T covers, Anchor in the middle). A patient empty raid is safe while you lead, but two in a row make the third a Do-or-Die. Aha: protecting a lead is its own skill — bank the safe single touch, spend the empty raids, and tackle only with the specialist whose hold matches his move. Finish ahead, never more than 2 behind.","mechanics":["game management","empty-raid counter","hold specialists","anchor","alternating raids"],"optimal":null,"branching":10,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":39,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: A o T K T o A (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Two-touch raider\": s 0.64 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 15/thigh 58/rush 27; toe: ankle 40/thigh 21/rush 29 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 15/thigh 39/block 23/rush 13; dash: ankle 24/thigh 19/block 44/rush 10 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 3 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 36/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 71/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist: a two-touch raider — after the first touch he turns for a second defender, so the defender in range changes mid-raid. Switch to whoever covers the new target (the tap-select is instant). Aha: defend the raider's NEXT target, not the last one. Stop 2 of 4 and concede no more than 3.","mechanics":["defender switch","hold specialists","anchor","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)"],"optimal":4,"branching":13,"trap":0,"explored":986},{"n":40,"grid":"[Match · spike · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: A T B R B T A · grip 0.90 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), B blocker (Dash risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: A T o K o T A (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 4 raids / 4 defences\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"League star\": s 0.70 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h27/t41 2T:h44/t31 3B:h39/t23 4R:h33/t30/k11 5B:h39/t23 6T:h44/t31 7A:h27/t41 bonus:62 | home after 1 touch: walk 58%, dash 63%, dubki 55% | after 2: walk 69%, dash 74%, dubki 66% | if held: pull 39%, lunge 38%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26; toe: ankle 45/thigh 16/rush 27 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 16/thigh 29/block 21/rush 12; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 41/rush 9; dubki: ankle 29/thigh 5/block 7/rush 12 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Concede at most 2\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 32/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 72/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Spike, every read at once: your specialist squad (A corners, T covers, Anchor) against a full league mat (A, T, B, R) and a Medium raider who reads your shape (no feints: the test is reading both ends, not bluffs). On your raids the mat has a counter for every move — Kick the R, Toe the T, Hand the A — no scouting here; on defence, match the specialist to his move. 4 raids each, win by 1.","mechanics":["hold specialists","anchor","backward kick","rusher defenders","blocker wall","ankle-catchers"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":41,"grid":"[Auction · combine · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Toe specialist\": s 0.12 · Easy · touches toe · home dubki · up to 1 touch\nAUCTION (purse 74): Corner(thigh corner) open 8 market 10-18; Corner(ankle corner) open 22 market 26-38; Anchor(anchor) open 16 market 18-30\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — toe: ankle 71/thigh 25/rush 43 | vs his way home — dubki: ankle 57/thigh 9/block 13/rush 24 | his touch lands 73% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 2 raids, buy Corner + Anchor | FAIL: opp scores > 5 | STARS: Win within his first 3 raids; Keep 10 lakh in the purse\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 72/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Combine auction and defence: the scouting report says their raider is a Toe-Touch specialist who Dubkis home — both beaten by Ankle holds. The Ankle Corner is the one you want, so the rival franchises bid him up; the Thigh Corner goes cheap and the Anchor sits between. 74 lakh buys the Ankle Corner and an Anchor only if you don't overpay. Aha: buy for the opponent you will face, not the bargain. Buy a Corner and an Anchor, then stop 2 of his 5 raids.","mechanics":["auction","hold specialists","anchor","ankle hold","thigh hold","scouting"],"optimal":11,"branching":2,"trap":null,"explored":36578},{"n":42,"grid":"[Auction · twist · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 0.90 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: auction only\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush hold\nON SCREEN: purse helper (still needed + cheapest squad left)\nAUCTION (purse 75): Anchor(anchor) open 18 market 34-48; Raider R8 open 25 market 28-46; Corner(ankle corner) open 12 market 14-26; Raider R5 open 12 market 12-24; Anchor(anchor) open 15 market 18-30\nRIVAL BIDDER: Harbour Hawks chase the FIRST Anchor (+14 lakh on his value), then stop\nGOAL: buy Raider + Anchor | STARS: Keep 10 lakh in the purse; Keep 18 lakh in the purse\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 39/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 68/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist, auction only — read the other bidder: the Harbour Hawks need an Anchor and chase the FIRST one on the list, paying about 14 lakh over his market value (shown in the lot's market range); once they have one they stop. You need a Raider and an Anchor from 75 lakh, and the purse helper shows the sum on every bid. Aha: let the rival overpay for the first Anchor — his twin later goes at market, and that saving buys the better Raider.","mechanics":["auction","rival bidder","player roles","anchor","purse"],"optimal":9,"branching":2,"trap":0,"explored":4894},{"n":43,"grid":"[Super Challenge · breather · Ch4 Auction Hall] OPP MAT: R o R o R o o · grip 0.38 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), o rookie · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raider reach 7 agi 6 spd 6\nFLOW: you raid 4x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h12/t11/k2 2o:h13/t12 3R:h13/t12/k3 4o:h13/t12 5R:h13/t12/k3 6o:h9/t9 7o:h4/t4 bonus:34 | home after 1 touch: walk 14%, dash 7%, dubki 13% | after 2: walk 19%, dash 9%, dubki 17% | if held: pull 52%, lunge 50%\nGOAL: score 4, 2x kick | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Land a bonus hop; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 40/40 (best 2★), a mid-skill player 83/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made.