r switch"],"optimal":null,"branching":2,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":45,"grid":"[Super Challenge · teach · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o o T o T o · grip 1.01 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h11/t10 2o:h15/t13 3o:h33/t14 4T:h47/t14 5o:h47/t14 6T:h47/t14 7o:h30/t10 bonus:11 | home after 1 touch: walk 47%, dash 25%, dubki 20% | after 2: walk 58%, dash 32%, dubki 26% | if held: pull 38%, lunge 37%\nGOAL: 1x superRaid | FAIL: raider out 3x | STARS: Never get caught; Super Raid on the first raid\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 31/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 62/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the Super Raid: three touches in one raid. Three touches take 21 of the 30 seconds and every touch makes the way home harder (depth ×1.7 at three). No scouting in this lesson, so only the route matters. Aha: string the touches along the rookie side first, then decide the way home before the clock runs out. Land a Super Raid within 3 raids.","mechanics":["super raid","raid clock","hand touch","toe touch","dubki","thigh-holders"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":46,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Continental raider\": s 0.55 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 50/rush 29/chain 47; toe: ankle 51/thigh 18/rush 31/chain 43 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 20/thigh 35/block 26/rush 15/chain 47; dash: ankle 32/thigh 17/block 49/rush 11/chain 41 | his touch lands 84% if untackled\nGOAL: 1x chain | FAIL: opp scores > 3 | STARS: Chain him within his first 2 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 86/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach the Chain Tackle: two adjacent defenders link — strong against every touch and every way home except the Dubki, and a chained raider rarely slips. Aha: two defenders, one chain — chain the pair around his target. Land a chain tackle in 5 raids and concede no more than 3 — one clean chain is the lesson, and a wrong pair costs a point.","mechanics":["chain tackle","ankle hold","thigh hold","block (defensive wall)","defender rush"],"optimal":2,"branching":18,"trap":0,"explored":63},{"n":47,"grid":"[Super Challenge · twist · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: - - o o o - - (3 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 3 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Super raider\": s 0.70 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26/chain 42; toe: ankle 45/thigh 16/rush 27/chain 39 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 16/thigh 29/block 21/rush 12/chain 40; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 41/rush 9/chain 34 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: 1x superTackle | FAIL: opp scores > 2 | STARS: Super Tackle with a chain; Concede nothing\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 82/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist: three rookies left in the middle of your mat, no specialists, against a raider who goes for two touches. Any tackle from 3 is a Super Tackle (+2), but a failed tackle on the touch costs two men and brings the all-out close. Aha: let the first touch go and chain him on the way home, when every tackle still counts as Super. Land a Super Tackle within 3 raids, concede no more than 2 — one bad read is survivable, two are not.","mechanics":["chain tackle","super tackle","super raid","all-out"],"optimal":2,"branching":11,"trap":0,"explored":40},{"n":48,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch5 Formation: Cage] OPP MAT: o C C o C C o · grip 1.02 · KEY: o rook