 vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach formation themes with the Cage: two chained pairs (C C) either side of the centre. Walking or dashing home past two chains is held most of the time; the Dubki ducks under both (READ). Aha: in the Cage, the way home is the puzzle. Score 4 in 5 raids — one spare raid to learn the Cage.","mechanics":["formation theme: Cage","chain links","dubki","toe touch","hand touch"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":49,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · twist · Ch5 Formation: Pincer] OPP MAT: T R o B o R T · grip 0.82 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), o rookie, B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1T:h44/t17 2R:h41/t27/k11 3o:h22/t20 4B:h15/t13 5o:h22/t20 6R:h41/t27/k11 7T:h44/t17 bonus:48 | home after 1 touch: walk 51%, dash 43%, dubki 25% | after 2: walk 62%, dash 54%, dubki 32% | if held: pull 40%, lunge 39%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Land a bonus hop; Score with a kick\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 30/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 72/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist theme, the Pincer: Thigh-holder corners and two Rushers just inside them squeeze the bonus line. The hop is a coin flip (about half held, READ) but a failed hop just ends the raid — while a Kick on a charging R (about 1 in 10 held) is the safe point and the Toe on the rookies (about 1 in 5) beats the T's. Aha: the bonus is worth taking only while all seven stand and only once; after a hop, kick the rushers. Score 4 in 5 raids, any way you like.","mechanics":["formation theme: Pincer","thigh-holders","rusher defenders","bonus line","backward kick"],"optimal":null,"branching":20,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":50,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o T o T o o · grip 1.05 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 4x · DRS reviews 2\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h12/t10 2o:h34/t14 3T:h48/t15 4o:h48/t15 5T:h48/t15 6o:h34/t14 7o:h12/t10 bonus:12 | home after 1 touch: walk 48%, dash 26%, dubki 21% | after 2: walk 59%, dash 33%, dubki 27% | if held: pull 37%, lunge 36%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Win a DRS review; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 2★), a mid-skill player 80/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach DRS on an easy mat, so the review is the only lesson: rookies with two Thigh-holders. Close touches are called by the referee and the call says how close: 'very tight' calls are wrong almost half the time, 'tight' ones 1 in 5. You have 2 reviews and a failed review is lost. Aha: review the very tight calls, accept the merely tight ones — a review is a resource, not a reflex. Score 4 in 4 raids — one point a raid, so a wrong call you don't review costs the trial.","mechanics":["DRS review","toe touch","hand touch","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":51,"grid":"[Ghost Duel · twist · Ch5 Formation: Ghost Gate] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 5 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: 