s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist: defend against a recorded ghost raider. Its 5 raids are known before you start (GHOST PLAN row: a Toe and Dash home, a Hand and walk, a bonus hop, a two-touch raid with a Dubki home, a corner Toe and Dash) and replay exactly — no feints — so the right counter is set up in advance and stops about 15 points more than usual (READ: Thigh v Hand, Ankle v Toe and Dubki, Rush v the hop, Block v the Dash, Chain v the walk). A chain tackle is the 3-star show but it costs two men if it breaks. Aha: a ghost can be solved: plan the perfect counter for each raid. Stop 3 of 5 and concede no more than 5.","mechanics":["ghost gate","chain tackle","block (defensive wall)","ankle hold","thigh hold","defender rush"],"optimal":null,"branching":15,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":52,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch5 Formation: Diamond] OPP MAT: o T R B R T o · grip 1.17 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on 