9%, dash 62%, dubki 18% | after 2: walk 80%, dash 73%, dubki 23% | if held: pull 39%, lunge 38%\nGOAL: beat the ghost's 5 points | FAIL: raider out 3x | STARS: Dubki home twice; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 37/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 63/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Spike: this week's ladder ghost raided the Cage (two chained pairs, T's at the corners) 5 times and scored 5 — the target is on the scoreboard all trial. Beat it (6+) in 5 raids. The chains make every walk or Dash home a risk, so Dubki home; one point a raid only ties the ghost, so at least one raid must take a greedy second touch, and every touch makes the way home deeper (READ: home after 1 vs after 2). Aha: choose WHICH raid is the greedy one — on the rookie in slot 4 and his chain-link neighbour, then duck home.","mechanics":["ghost duel","formation theme: Cage","chain links","raid depth","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":54,"grid":"[Super Challenge · breather · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o o o T o o o · grip 0.69 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · no scouting on this trial (no SCOUTED tags)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 3x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h8/t7 2o:h10/t9 3o:h24/t9 4T:h35/t10 5o:h24/t9 6o:h10/t9 7o:h8/t7 bonus:8 | home after 1 touch: walk 25%, dash 15%, dubki 14% | after 2: walk 32%, dash 19%, dubki 18% | if held: pull 41%, lunge 41%\nGOAL: 1x superRaid | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Super Raid on the first raid; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 69/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Breather with a toy, after the ghost spike: the fan-zone Super Raid booth. A young side (rookies and one T) that never scouts you, three raids, and the crowd wants a Super Raid — three touches in one raid, home before the 30 s clock. Aha: the three-touch route that was a long shot in trial 45 is a show on a soft mat — take the rookies in a line and duck home.","mechanics":["super raid","raid clock","dubki","score attack"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":55,"grid":"[Full Match · boss · Ch5 Continental Cup] OPP MAT: o C C o C C o · grip 1.48 · KEY: o rookie, C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raider reach 7 agi 6 spd 6\nFLOW: alternate raids 05:00→20:00 (~21 raids in all, ~11 each, half-time swap at 10:00) · start score 4-6 · DRS reviews 1\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Continental captain\": s 0.69 · Medium · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · feints 15%\nMOMENT (reversal, at half-time): \"HALF-TIME REVERSAL! They drop the Cage for an Ankle Line — four Ankle-catchers read the Dubki and the Toe.\" → OPP MAT becomes A T A o A T A (new: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky))\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h20/t18 2C:h32/t29 3C:h32/t29 4o:h28/t25 5C:h32/t29 6C:h32/t29 7o:h20/t18 bonus:15 | home after 1 touch: walk 73%, dash 74%, dubki 26% | after 2: walk 83%, dash 84%, dubki 33% | if held: pull 22%, lunge 19%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26/chain 43; toe: ankle 45/thigh 16/rush 28/chain 39; bonus: ankle 28/thigh 18/rush 48/chain 25 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 17/thigh 29/block 22/rush 12/chain 40; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 41/rush 9/chain 35; dubki: ankle 30/thigh 5/block 7/rush 12/chain 11 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 4; Win a DRS review\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 54/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + 