ers with two Thigh-holders) that reads the Dubki and the Toe, so the Hand on an A and the Dash home come back — and the T's still punish the walk. Their raider feints 15% and takes two touches (chain the return). One DRS review. Aha: the half-time whistle changes the answer — the move that won the first half loses the second. Win the match.","mechanics":["full match","chain tackle","super raid","DRS review","formation theme: Cage","ankle-catchers","feints","mid-match reversal"],"optimal":null,"branching":18,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":56,"grid":"[Match · teach · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o T R B R T o · grip 1.30 · KEY: o rookie, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), B blocker (Dash risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~9 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raiders Veer R8 A7 S7 st3, Kabir R6 A6 S5 st8 (fatigue)\nFLOW: alternate: 6 raids / 6 defences\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"World raider\": s 0.55 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h34/t12 2T:h59/t27 3R:h54/t37/k17 4B:h41/t38 5R:h54/t37/k17 6T:h59/t27 7o:h34/t12 bonus:55 | home after 1 touch: walk 66%, dash 56%, dubki 34% | after 2: walk 77%, dash 66%, dubki 43% | if held: pull 48%, lunge 39%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 50/rush 29/chain 47; toe: ankle 51/thigh 18/rush 31/chain 43 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 20/thigh 35/block 26/rush 15/chain 47; dash: ankle 32/thigh 17/block 49/rush 11/chain 41; dubki: ankle 36/thigh 6/block 9/rush 15/chain 13 | his touch lands 84% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 3+ | STARS: Win by 5; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 33/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 70/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content u