A tired raider reaches less and is held more. Aha: rotate — the star for the big raids, the workhorse in between. 6 raids each, win by 3.","mechanics":["fatigue","raider rotation","chain tackle","super raid","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":2,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":57,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · teach · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: - T A K A T - (captain weak to kick) · grip 0.50 · KEY: T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), K captain · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~9 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 5x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 2T:h25/t16 3A:h24/t33 4K:h22/t38/k7 5A:h24/t33 6T:h25/t16 | home after 1 touch: walk 37%, dash 24%, dubki 40% | after 2: walk 47%, dash 31%, dubki 50% | if held: pull 40%, lunge 39%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Score with a kick on the captain; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 31/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 75/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Teach rival captains: five on their mat (so the bonus line is dead) and their captain K anchors the centre — every move near him is dangerous and he guards every way home. His one weakness: he chases, so a Backward Kick on him is the safest touch on the mat (READ k on slot 4), and the kick tags him out of the way home too. Aha: kick the captain, don't avoid him. Score 4 in 5 raids.","mechanics":["rival captain","backward kick","ankle-catchers","thigh-holders","dubki"],"optimal":null,"branching":14,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":58,"grid":"[Defend Stand · teach · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 6 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"The Dubki King\": s 0.55 · Hard · touches hand/toe · home dubki · up to 2 touches\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 50/rush 29/chain 47; toe: ankle 51/thigh 18/rush 31/chain 43 | vs his way home — dubki: ankle 36/thigh 6/block 9/rush 15/chain 13 | his touch lands 84% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 4 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Concede at most 1\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 33/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 79/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Rival raider: the Dubki King always ducks home — under thighs, chains and walls. Only the Ankle Hold reads the dubki — the best answer on the board (READ). Aha: a signature move is a promise — let the touch go and ankle him on the way home. Stop 3 of 6 and concede no more than 4.","mechanics":["rival raider signature","ankle hold","chain tackle","block (defensive wall)","thigh hold"],"optimal":null,"branching":11,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":59,"grid":"[Defend Stand · twist · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.00 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o C K C o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 6 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"The Feint Master\": s 0.59 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 1 touch · feints 20% · TELL on 75% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 94%)\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 19/thigh 48/rush 28/chain 56; toe: ankle 49/thigh 17/rush 30/chain 51 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 19/thigh 33/block 27/rush 14/chain 55; dash: ankle 30/thigh 16/block 51/rush 10/chain 48; dubki: ankle 34/thigh 6/block 9/rush 14/chain 15 | his touch lands 85% if untackled\nGOAL: stop 3 raids | FAIL: opp scores > 3 | STARS: Win within his first 4 raids; Two chain tackles\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 28/40 (best 2★), a mid-skill player 66/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Twist on rival raiders: the Feint Master feints 1 raid in 5 and, like every feinter since trial 37, has a tell: on 3 of 4 feints his hips turn before the shown move and the telegraph flickers (FEINT? on screen) — then the shown move is a lie. With no tell, the telegraph is true about 19 times in 20. Your Anchor stands between two Covers, so a chain through the centre is strong whichever touch is real, and the Ankle covers both his Dash and his Dubki home. Aha: read the tell — trust a clean telegraph, and against a flicker use the move that has no weakness. Stop 3 of his 6 raids, concede no more than 3.","mechanics":["feints","feint tell","rival raider signature","chain tackle","anchor","ankle hold"],"optimal":null,"branching":15,"trap":0,"explored":40000},{"n":60,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: R T o K o T R (captain weak to toe) · grip 1.26 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), o rookie, K captain · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~7 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raiders Veer R8 A7 S7 st3, Kabir R6 A6 S5 st8, Dev R6 A7 S6 st6 (fatigue)\nFLOW: alternate raids 30:00→40:00 (~14 raids in all, ~7 each) · start score 16-18\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"World raider\": s 0.65 · Medium · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · feints 15% · TELL on 50% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 92%)\nMOMENT (reversal, after raid 6): \"Their captain is tired and goes to the bench — a fresh Rusher takes the centre.\" → OPP MAT becomes R T o R o T R\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h49/t32/k11 2T:h58/t26 3o:h48/t14 4K:h44/t13/k43 5o:h48/t14 6T:h58/t26 7R:h49/t32/k11 bonus:72 | home after 1 touch: walk 72%, dash 49%, dubki 51% | after 2: walk 82%, dash 59%, dubki 62% | if held: pull 39%, lunge 30%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27/chain 44; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29/chain 40; bonus: ankle 29/thigh 19/rush 50/chain 26 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13/chain 42; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 43/rush 10/chain 37; dubki: ankle 32/thigh 5/block 8/rush 13/chain 11 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 33/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 62/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Combine fatigue with a reversal: the last 10 minutes of a group match (~14 raids), 16-18 down, with three raiders to rotate (one star, two workhorses) against a mat anchored by a rival captain weak to the Toe Touch, with rookies either side of him so his Toe gem is the safest on the mat. After 6 raids their captain tires and goes to the bench: a fresh Rusher takes the centre, so the captain's Toe weakness is gone and the Kick on the charging R becomes the centre's safe touch. Aha: rest the star for the raids after the swap, and re-read the centre when the captain leaves. Win by 1.","mechanics":["defence reads repeats","fatigue","raider rotation","rival captain","backward kick","chain tackle","dubki","mid-match reversal"],"optimal":null,"branching":3,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":61,"grid":"[Raid Puzzle · combine · Ch6 Formation: Cage] OPP MAT: o C C K T T o (captain weak to dash) · grip 0.85 · KEY: o rookie, C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired), K captain, T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky) · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~9 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you raid 6x\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1o:h13/t11 2C:h21/t19 3C:h32/t30 4K:h48/t36/k38 5T:h59/t24 6T:h52/t12 7o:h26/t9 bonus:10 | home after 1 touch: walk 66%, dash 44%, dubki 35% | after 2: walk 76%, dash 55%, dubki 44% | if held: pull 33%, lunge 32%\nGOAL: score 4 | FAIL: raider out 2x | STARS: Land a Super Raid; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 34/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 76/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Combine: a half-Cage with a rival captain at its hinge — a chained pair on the left, the captain in the centre, two T's on the right. Two ways home compete (READ): the Dubki ducks under the chain and the T's but not the captain; the Dash is the captain's weakness (he cannot turn) but runs into the chain. And the answer moves: every chain link you put out breaks the chain for the next raid, so the Dash gets safer raid by raid. Aha: there is no fixed answer — re-price the way home after every raid. Score 4 in 6 raids; a Super Raid is the 3-star swing.","mechanics":["rival captain","formation theme: Cage","chain links","dubki","dash home","backward kick","super raid"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":62,"grid":"[Match · combine · Ch6 Formation: Wall] OPP MAT: B B o K o B B (captain weak to toe) · grip 1.10 · KEY: B blocker (Dash risky), o rookie, K captain · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~9 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: alternate: 5 raids / 5 defences · start score 9-11\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"World raider\": s 0.65 · Medium · touches hand/toe · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches\nON SCREEN: Blocker wall drawn on the midline; the Dash gem carries a WALLED tag with its real % (shown, never a hidden trap)\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1B:h18/t15 2B:h21/t18 3o:h32/t15 4K:h42/t12/k42 5o:h32/t15 6B:h21/t18 7B:h18/t15 bonus:16 | home after 1 touch: walk 61%, dash 90%, dubki 45% | after 2: walk 72%, dash 95%, dubki 55% | if held: pull 28%, lunge 27%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 18/thigh 46/rush 27/chain 44; toe: ankle 47/thigh 17/rush 29/chain 40 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 18/thigh 31/block 23/rush 13/chain 42; dash: ankle 28/thigh 15/block 44/rush 10/chain 37; dubki: ankle 32/thigh 5/block 8/rush 13/chain 11 | his touch lands 86% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 3; Never get caught\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 33/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 66/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Combine with the Wall theme: four Blockers link arms on the midline around a captain weak to the Toe Touch, with rookies beside him, against a Medium raider who never feints. The Dash gem is drawn WALLED — it is legal but the wall eats it (READ) — so the way home is the walk or the Dubki, and the Wall reads the one you used last raid (SCOUTED). The Dubki is the low-% way home (READ) — and exactly the move they scout, so after a Dubki raid the walk becomes the better price for one raid; the walk deepens fast after two touches. Aha: alternate the way home and keep the walk for single-touch raids right after a scouted Dubki. Joined at 9-11 down, 5 raids each, win by 1.","mechanics":["formation theme: Wall","rival captain","blocker wall","defence reads repeats","chain tackle"],"optimal":null,"branching":19,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":63,"grid":"[Super Challenge · breather · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: o o o o o o o · grip 1.29 · KEY: o rookie\nMY SIDE: o o C K C o o (7 on mat)\nFLOW: you defend 4 CPU raids\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Veteran raider\": s 0.45 · Easy · touches hand/toe · home walk · up to 1 touch\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 21/thigh 54/rush 31/chain 61; toe: ankle 55/thigh 19/rush 34/chain 56 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 22/thigh 39/block 31/rush 17/chain 64 | his touch lands 81% if untackled\nGOAL: 1x chain | FAIL: opp scores > 1 | STARS: Chain him within his first 2 raids; Concede nothing\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 35/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 74/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick 