,"grid":"[Comeback · spike · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: R T A K A T R (captain weak to kick) · grip 1.10 · KEY: R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), T thigh-holder (Hand/walk risky), A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), K captain · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~4 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raiders Veer R8 A7 S7 st6, Kabir R6 A6 S5 st8 (fatigue)\nFLOW: alternate raids 30:00→40:00 (~14 raids in all, ~7 each) · start score 18-19\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"Champion raider\": s 0.69 · Hard · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · feints 20% · TELL on 50% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 89%)\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1R:h45/t29/k10 2T:h53/t40 3A:h43/t55 4K:h39/t62/k14 5A:h43/t55 6T:h53/t40 7R:h45/t29/k10 bonus:67 | home after 1 touch: walk 70%, dash 45%, dubki 70% | after 2: walk 80%, dash 56%, dubki 80% | if held: pull 42%, lunge 33%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26/chain 42; toe: ankle 45/thigh 16/rush 27/chain 39; bonus: ankle 27/thigh 18/rush 48/chain 25 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 16/thigh 29/block 21/rush 12/chain 40; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 41/rush 9/chain 35; dubki: ankle 30/thigh 5/block 7/rush 12/chain 11 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 4; Score with 2 Kicks\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 32/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 72/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Spike: the last 10 minutes of the World semi-final (~15 raids), 18-19 down, against the champions' feinting raider (1 in 5, half of them with the tell) and a captain weak to the Kick, with two raiders to rotate. No DRS and only light scouting — the test is fatigue and the feint read. Fatigue is the clock inside the clock: Veer is the better raider but tires, Kabir never does; the Kick on the captain is the lowest-% held touch on the mat but it lands only about 2 times in 3 (a miss is an empty raid, READ). Aha: spend the star only where the captain's Kick weakness pays, and save a fresh Veer for the last three raids. Win by 1.","mechanics":["fatigue","raider rotation","rival captain","feints","backward kick","chain tackle"],"optimal":null,"branching":2,"trap":null,"explored":40000},{"n":66,"grid":"[Full Match · boss · Ch6 World Championship] OPP MAT: A C R K R C A (captain weak to kick) · grip 1.59 · KEY: A ankle-catcher (Toe/hop/Dubki risky), C chain link (walk/Dash risky when paired), R rusher (touch/hop risky, Kick safe), K captain · SCOUTED: a move from your last raid is tagged on its gem and ~4 pts more likely held (capped, same on every mat)\nMY SIDE: o o o o o o o (7 on mat) · raiders Veer R8 A7 S7 st4, Kabir R6 A6 S5 st8, Dev R6 A7 S6 st6 (fatigue)\nFLOW: alternate raids 01:00→12:00 (~15 raids in all, ~8 each, half-time swap at 06:00) · start score 0-2\nMY MOVES: hand toe kick bonus walk dash dubki pull lunge | DEFENCE: ankle thigh block rush chain hold\nCPU RAIDER \"World captain\": s 0.70 · Hard · touches hand/toe/bonus · home walk/dash/dubki · up to 2 touches · feints 25% · TELL on 50% of feints (telegraph flickers → it is a lie; a clean telegraph is true 86%)\nREAD (gem % held) touch: 1A:h19/t59 2C:h40/t56 3R:h59/t57/k17 4K:h66/t65/k11 5R:h59/t57/k17 6C:h40/t56 7A:h19/t59 bonus:86 | home after 1 touch: walk 67%, dash 51%, dubki 82% | after 2: walk 77%, dash 62%, dubki 90% | if held: pull 32%, lunge 23%\nREAD (gem % stop, made by the cover): vs his touch — hand: ankle 17/thigh 44/rush 26/chain 42; toe: ankle 45/thigh 16/rush 27/chain 39; bonus: ankle 27/thigh 18/rush 47/chain 25 | vs his way home — walk: ankle 16/thigh 29/block 21/rush 12/chain 40; dash: ankle 26/thigh 14/block 41/rush 9/chain 34; dubki: ankle 29/thigh 5/block 7/rush 12/chain 11 | his touch lands 87% if untackled\nGOAL: win by 1+ | STARS: Win by 4; Two chain tackles\nPROOF (validate, real engine, fresh match seeds): a competent player won 33/40 (best 3★), a mid-skill player 58/100","legend":"KABADDI RAID TRIAL (content unit; the player raids and defends in turns). OPP MAT = 7 defender slots, left corner → right corner ('-' = out). Defender traits: o rookie; T Thigh-holder (beats Hand Touch + walking home); A Ankle-catcher (beats Toe Touch, bonus hop, Dubki); B Blocker (midline wall, beats the Dash home); R Rusher (charges: beats hops and touches; a Backward Kick tags him); C Chain link (two adjacent C's chain: beat walk/dash home, Dubki ducks under); K rival captain (strong at everything except his one listed weakness). Danger comes from the target and his neighbours and grows with every touch already made. SCOUTED: only on trials whose OPP MAT row says SCOUTED, a move used on my previous raid is read — its gem shows a SCOUTED tag and the higher % (capped at ~8 points); rows that say 'no scouting' never show the tag. READ rows = the % the game shows on each option gem, never a recommendation (h/t/k = Hand/Toe/Kick touch on that slot). My raid: touch beats (7 s) + optional bonus hop (5 s, 6+ defenders) + way home (6 s) inside the 30 s raid clock; held → struggle (pull or lunge). My defence vs the CPU raider's telegraphed move: Ankle, Thigh, Rush (by a defender within two of his target), Chain (two adjacent), Block (way home only), Hold (no tackle; vs a real Kick it is the step-back counter). Feints: a feinting raider's telegraph lies at his feint rate; a TELL (FEINT? flicker) marks some feints openly. MOMENT = a one-off referee call or mid-match reversal that changes the mat/raider. MY SIDE roles: A ankle / T thigh specialist, C cover, K anchor, R rusher. Rules: 1 point per touch, tackle 1 (Super Tackle 2 with ≤3 defenders), bonus only with 6+ defenders, all-out +2, every point revives one, the 3rd straight empty raid is Do-or-Die. CPU: skill s, Easy/Medium/Hard brain. PROOF = validate's simulated players on the real engine over 40/100 match seeds.","intent":"Final boss, a mastery test of three things only, as a World Final Blitz of 2x6 game minutes, joined at 1:00 already 0-2 down after their captain's opening two-touch raid (~15 raids): (1) their captain anchors a Pincer-Cage mat and is weak to the Kick, (2) their raider is the Feint Master (1 feint in 4) — and in the final he hides his tell better than in trial 59: only half his feints flicker who goes for two touches, (3) you rotate three raiders through fatigue. No DRS, light scouting. Aha: the final asks for the chapter lessons in one match — kick the captain, trust a clean telegraph and chain the pair around his target, save a fresh Veer for the closing raids. Win by 1 — from 0-2 that is a three-point swing: a final is won, not survived.","mechanics":["full match","rival captain","rival raider signature","feints","feint tell","fatigue","raider rotation","chain tackle"],"optimal":null,"branching":3,"trap":null,"explored":40000}]}
